note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note gpu/amd/rest/gate.om: OMEGA-GPU-AMD-REST, the checks CUDApp ran in shell and Python for the AMD gfx942 back end,
note rewritten in seeded Omega (Linux AArch64). The old instruments stay in CUDApp as oracles; their recorded verdicts
note are the four *-verdicts.tsv / *-sections.tsv tables beside this file (generated, see README.md).
note Build from the repository root (OM-2 program mode; seed/ng/sha256.om supplies sh_dat, sh_all, sh_dig):
note   { printf 'om2\n'; cat seed/ng/sha256.om gpu/amd/rest/gate.om; } | seed/out/omc > gate
note Run from the repository root: gate OMC SCRATCH
note OMC      the compiler under test; its sha256 must equal the first word of seed/out/omc.sha256, or nothing runs
note          (exit 69, nothing written)
note SCRATCH  a new directory (created 0700), at most 1024 bytes of path; an existing one is refused (exit 2)
note 1. llvm-mc parity (was tests/amd/run.sh with llvm-objcopy, dd, awk). For each row of llvm18-sections.tsv the
note    writer builds gpu/amd/gfx942/K.isa; .text and .note bytes, rodata[0,16) and rodata[24,end) hash as
note    llvm-mc-18 made them from K-gfx942.s; rodata[16,24) equals sym(K) - sym(K.kd); e_flags is 0x54C.
note 2. Launcher verdicts (was tests/amd-kfd-launch/check.py, CPU part). launch-verdicts.tsv: every object hashes
note    as check.py built it; each mutated object and input file is rebuilt here and hashes as check.py's input did;
note    each plan unit is composed here and hashes as check.py's unit did; each run row gives check.py's exit,
note    stdout and stderr. x86 rows run under /usr/bin/qemu-x86_64 (NOT_RUN without it). Rows whose verb is vadd or
note    run would open /dev/kfd: they run only when /dev/kfd is absent (the absent-device verdict), else NOT_RUN.
note 3. Writer verdicts (was tests/amd/{branches,formats,boundaries}.py and the MessagePack part of run.sh).
note    writer-verdicts.tsv: each SOPP and format table is generated here and hashes as the oracle's did; the
note    writer's exit and bytes match; the MessagePack probe main is generated here and hashes as boundaries.py's;
note    the spec bytes computed here hash as boundaries.py's; hsaco.om's encoder emits exactly them.
note 4. Controls, each must be caught: a compiler one byte longer; vadd.isa with "I 5 260 8 4 0x01 " changed to 261;
note    a llvm table digest changed; an object with no llvm row; a launcher verdict with its expected bytes changed;
note    two MessagePack encoder mutants (they compile and run, the bytes differ); the loader refusing a wrong
note    machine (exit 33) and a truncated object (exit 34); the wrong-request table must differ from the header
note    oracle; records.om without its 2^64-1 index guard must exit 0 there (the table says 3); a kfd verdict with
note    its expected stderr changed.
note 5. KFD host verdicts (was tests/amd-kfd/{run.sh,oracle.py}, CPU part). kfd-verdicts.tsv: requests.tsv has
note    the numbers the C sizeof/offsetof oracle printed, line for line; aql, kernarg, records and ring (unit +
note    cli.om) build twice to the oracle's bytes; the three mutated tables and the over-fuel table are written
note    here and hash as oracle.py's; each devctl allowlist program is refused by omc as recorded (exit 9); each
note    run row gives oracle.py's exit, stdout and stderr.
note Output: one line per check, then OMEGA-GPU-AMD-REST PASS|FAIL sections=S objects=O verdicts=V not_run=N
note writer=W kfd=F controls=C caught=K hardware=NOT_RUN. Exit 0 PASS, 1 FAIL, 2 bad usage or setup, 69 refused.
note Buffers: inputs are read into fixed 16 MiB (objects, tables made here) and 1 MiB (verdict tables) buffers; a
note larger input fails its check by name, never truncates silently.
